  "question": {
    "text": "The eccentricity of an ellipse, with its centre at the origin, is $\\frac{1}{2}$. If one of the directrices is $x=$ 4 , then the equation of the ellipse is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$3 x^2+4 y^2=1$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$3 x^2+4 y^2=12$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$4 x^2+3 y^2=12$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$4 x^2+3 y^2=1$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Equation of directrix is $x=a / e=4 \\Rightarrow a=2$\n$$\nb^2=a^2\\left(1-e^2\\right) \\Rightarrow b^2=3\n$$\nHence equation of ellipse is $3 x^2+4 y^2=12$"
  }
}